      "How old are you? In most countries the question has a single answer, but in South Korea it long had several. Under the traditional way of counting, a baby was already one year old at birth, and everyone became a year older together on New Year's Day. Officials, doctors and courts, however, generally used the international method, counting full years from the day of birth. A third method, based simply on the year of birth, was also used in some laws. In June 2023, the government tried to settle the matter by law, and the change has prompted a wider question about whether a state should tell people how to count their own age.",
